DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(x-10)^2+5*(x^2)+3");
$fun_1 = Formula("(sin(x))*1");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("{0, 1} U [2, 8] U {-7, -1, 3}");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("([2, 8]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [2, 8]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({0, 1}))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[1, 14] U [1, 14] U [1, 14] U ((0, 12) U (0, 12) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (((0, 12)) U ({-10, -8, -4, 9}))))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(0, 12) U [1, 14] U [1, 14]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`14.27+4+15/1`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(33.27),width=>9}
---

[`10.48+7/16.`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>10.9175,width=>9}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 0 < x < 12\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -8, -4, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup C \cup C \cup (A \cup A \cap ((A) \cup (B))) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 8\}`]
- [`B = \{0, 1\}`]
- [`C = \{-7, -1, 3\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A) \cap A \cap (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, 0, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, -2, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, -2, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, 0, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, 0, -5>") . Compute("<8, -2, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<0, 0, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -4, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, 2, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 8, 5, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -4, -8>") . Compute("<8, 5, -2>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 5, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -4, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 2, -6>") . Compute("<-4, -4, -8>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, -4, -8>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, 2, -6>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>5)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
